{
  "helped": [
    {"anchor": "inputs/brief.md:3-12", "note": "Exact sdd-new invocation and exact sdd-check command removed all command guessing; call_01_MjKuJuCcIDLPAZpWBU2Z8633 and call_00_k5lSGOHvWGOX7ycsNwmN0250 ran as written."},
    {"anchor": "ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml STEP_2_FILL", "note": "Per-section recipes plus the one-whole-Write rule gave a clear fill order; the skeleton manifest listed required vs optional sections."},
    {"anchor": "ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/entity-inventory-format.xml, entity-surface-format.xml, dbc-contracts.xml, requirement-entry-format.xml", "note": "Concrete table/field shapes let the DbC, inventory and requirement blocks be authored once and pass the checker."},
    {"anchor": "npx --no-install gennady sdd-check --spec ... --authoring (call_00_k5lSGOHvWGOX7ycsNwmN0250)", "note": "Returned the two real defects by name: SDD_AUTHORING_PLACEHOLDER at line 199 and SDD_REQ_ACRONYM_MISMATCH naming NOR as the expected acronym."},
    {"anchor": "specs/infra-base/infra-base.spec.md, specs/token/token.spec.md", "note": "Seeded language/format examples made the Russian operator-facing register and pending-operator handoff shape unambiguous."}
  ],
  "friction": [
    {"anchor": "ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml STEP_2_FILL / entity-surface-format.xml", "note": "No instruction states how deep a relative link to a file outside specs/ must climb. I wrote ../../../docs/token-contract.md, resolved by the host as specs/docs/token-contract.md (call_00_njLvh4OG9QC9Ng6fdsCS3011). Correct depth from specs/token/pipeline/normalize is ../../../../docs/token-contract.md. The owner recipe only covers links within specs (../ per --module segment)."},
    {"anchor": "sdd-check --spec --authoring (call_00_7vCTLDhMavVTPbukdIEM9906)", "note": "Reported 'clean / authoring-boundary: ready' while the link was broken; the link class is only caught by the independent host oracle. So the CLI receipt cannot be read as link validation."},
    {"anchor": "ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml AX_REQ_DL_ID_GRAMMAR reference", "note": "Requirement acronym derivation (NOR from filename) is not stated in module.directive or the skeleton; the first write used NORM and needed a second whole-write. Not resolved whether AX_REQ_DL_ID_GRAMMAR documents it — I did not read it (unknown)."},
    {"anchor": "write call_00_njLvh4OG9QC9Ng6fdsCS3011", "note": "Avoidable second whole-write: I left the '<!-- Optional appendix — include only when ... -->' comment in place, which the checker flagged as SDD_AUTHORING_PLACEHOLDER. Skeleton said replace every guidance comment; I overlooked one. A pre-write grep for '<!--' would have caught it."},
    {"anchor": "call_00_4NZb3DYROZ7nUF8hGTC00652 and call_01_5m6gLxiqKS3odAN6czAj5234", "note": "Two separate sed ranges into root.directive.xml for DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT; one targeted read would have sufficed. Mild, not a defect."}
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "Whether the host oracle requires a markdown link to docs/token-contract.md at all, or a plain-text/code-span reference to an out-of-specs file would pass.",
    "Whether the correct link depth for outside-specs targets is specified anywhere I did not read (unknown; not verified).",
    "Whether AX_REQ_DL_ID_GRAMMAR specifies the acronym derivation, which would have prevented the first whole-write."
  ],
  "nextHypothesis": "Test an added STEP_2_FILL instruction stating the link rule: relative paths are computed from the spec's own directory, so a target outside specs/ climbs ../../../../ (four segments for a two-segment --module) to the repo root. Also add a pre-write check for any residual '<!--' guidance comment before the single Write. Expected effect: no second whole-write and a clean relative-links host check."
}
